# App contract quick reference

| Task | Entry point |
| --- | --- |
| Find apps in a workspace | `us compatibility list -o .` |
| Read selected features/runtime | `<app>/.unstoppable/project.json` |
| Review dependency/runtime differences | `us compatibility check -o <app>` |
| Desktop networking/storage/IPC commands | `worker.js` |
| Desktop browser UI | `app/index.js` and `app/bridge.js` |
| Node networking/storage | `src/swarm-manager.ts` and `src/storage-manager.ts` |
| Node local AI | `src/ai-manager.ts` |
| Maintained local AI contract | `.unstoppable/runtime-ai/index.js` |
| Experimental Expo UI/worklet | `app/index.tsx`, `bare/index.js` |
| New shared JSON / collaboration | `@unstoppable-stack/p2p/data`; `modules/managed-data.mdc` |
| New remote services | `@unstoppable-stack/p2p/service` and `/rpc`; `modules/p2p.mdc` |
| Existing resource mirroring | `@unstoppable-stack/p2p/sync` on the existing node/store |
| Installed dependency versions | lockfile and package metadata |

Do not assume legacy `src/p2p/` component classes exist. Read the generated files before importing helpers. The compatibility table is generated from the same manifest as package declarations; use the installed app's recorded profile instead of a universal latest-version table.

AI session: `load(options)`, `stream(history, { requestId, signal, onTrim })`, `cancel(requestId)`, `close()`. The app owns history. A session has one active inference; Stop cancels native work and waits for settlement before reuse. Mock tokens stay labeled.

Detailed SDK APIs: https://docs.qvac.tether.io/sdk/js-ts-sdk/ and https://docs.holepunch.to/. Use installed types and release notes matching the app's version.
